{
  "dom_id": "step-q338390",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{t\\to -1}(\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}})=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the sum and root rules, we get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to -1}(\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}}) & ={lim}_{t\\to -1}\\sqrt[7]{(2t+1)^{7}}-{lim}_{t\\to -1}\\sqrt[3]{({t}^{2}+t+1)^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{{({lim}_{t\\to -1}(2t+1))}^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{{({lim}_{t\\to -1}({t}^{2}+t+1))}^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(2(-1)+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{(((-1)^{2}+(-1)+1))^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(-2+1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{((1-1+1))^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{(-1)^{7}}-\\sqrt[3]{(1)^{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[7]{-1}-\\sqrt[3]{1} \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
